Subject: Keep repeated symbol lookup out of the giant startup function
Origin: Filnix
Upstream-Status: Not submitted

Same change as sdl2-symbol-loader.patch: LoadSDL20Symbol is otherwise
inlined into the startup function once per SDL2 symbol. With Fil-C's
Clang at -O3, SDL12_compat.c took 873 s and 3.8 GB; with this, 30 s and
0.3 GB.

--- a/src/SDL12_compat.c
+++ b/src/SDL12_compat.c
@@ -1355,7 +1355,9 @@
 #define DIRSEP "/"
 #endif
 
-static void *
+/* Inlining this for every SDL2 symbol makes Fil-C's instrumented startup
+ * function prohibitively expensive for LLVM's scalar replacement pass. */
+static __attribute__((noinline)) void *
 LoadSDL20Symbol(const char *fn, int *okay)
 {
     void *retval = NULL;
